The calibration locator grammar is `<root-file>::json-fence[schema=<schema>,id=<id>]`; `root-file` must be a regular file already permitted by the Archive Contract root allowlist, and this locator names `plan.md`. Resolution opens that file, scans only fences whose opening line is three backticks followed immediately by `json`, strict-parses each payload as JSON, and selects by exact top-level `schema` and `id`. Exactly one match is required. A missing file or absent `id` is `path-not-found`; more than one exact match is `duplicate-target`; the requested `id` found only under another schema is `wrong-schema`. The resolved report hash is SHA-256 over UTF-8 canonical JSON with sorted keys, compact separators, and one trailing LF. It is a sub-block hash, not a hash of `plan.md`, so it has no self-reference. The block below is final before review and is never generated or changed after final review.

```json
